-- WW.seg: what each declaration's informal text opens.
-- Notation (opened to expose the shape of a type: "A x", a pair, a bar):
--   Cl Cap Sub Eqv Iff Bar Seg OTc tau M scA TH idx BndE PsiP H24 Mx Dn, the class
--   definitions the text names: Lf (a set as a class), WW (Def. 4.25), Cov (4.28(a)),
--   CardOf, and Ag, WA (A [= W(A), x in W(A)).
-- The two levels (sets at ul, classes at ul+) have equal predicates by definition:
--   OK, LT, Tr, Cap, Lf, opened once, in ok-up/ok-dn, lt-up/lt-dn, cap-up/cap-dn.
-- Definitions opened where the text says "by definition":
--   card at a sum (card-cons, card-add: the values of the head) and at phi' (card-phi:
--   card (phi y z) = ifQ (le z y) (card y) (card z), which evaluates le, as in
--   Clos.card-phi); up (up-of: x+ is the second card value); ww-set (the parts of
--   y in WW, ww-sag, ww-mem, ww-up).
-- Lemmas 4.30, 4.31 (notation as above, plus H430 (the hypotheses of 4.30), Cu, Cua (the
-- sets C, C u {a}), Emp, Bom, Bw (the sets B), Om431 (the predicate of the induction), Fb
-- (the hypotheses of fi-ww), Prog, Mid, InC, GH, G1, G2, NFom, PsiP, DCard, USum, WDo,
-- BndE).  Definitions opened where the text says "by definition" or "computation":
--   cu-g (the set of x in B, in cu-gag, cu-in, cu-eq), ww-set (h-w, ww-low, s-cap);
--   mI (mI-lo); omF (Omega_I = I in om-I, Omega_d = d in w-lt, Omega^{n+1} in w-ww,
--   w-mono); omN, suc (W_{n+1} = Omega_{W_n}, x+1 = x + 1); ifT isI (Omega_d, I = I);
--   one (1 = phi_0 0 in xs-in, fb0); phiF crit and isZero isG (phi_0 0 = 1, ww-one);
--   hd isA (the head of (c, 1), lt-sucS); the computations 0 <' I (h430-zero: lt cmp2
--   fwd cl1 other) and psi_I 0 in OT (ok-psiI0: isOT isR allLt G and); 0 + 1 = 1 (fb0:
--   add isZero isOne).
